{"_id":"68a7360d8ec3d8323af1290a","nodeId":"E9HR_voxQ2a2tvWUuva_p","roadmapSlug":"blockchain","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:53.730Z","description":"# Decentralization vs. Trust\n\nDecentralization refers to the distribution of power and control away from a central authority. Trust, in this context, is the reliance on a third party or system to act honestly and reliably. The relationship between the two lies in how decentralization aims to reduce or eliminate the need for trust in a single entity by distributing it across a network.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What Crypto Is Really About","url":"https://blog.chain.link/what-crypto-is-really-about/","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a1af"},{"type":"article","title":"Ethereum Consensus Mechanisms","url":"https://ethereum.org/en/developers/docs/consensus-mechanisms/","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a1b0"},{"type":"video","title":"The Superiority of Cryptographic Truth","url":"https://youtu.be/AEtBPbmIRKQ","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a1b1"},{"type":"feed","title":"Explore top posts about Decentralization","url":"https://app.daily.dev/tags/decentralization?ref=roadmapsh","_id":"6a7f4f5dcb44947debd1a1b2"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:24:45.750Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/blockchain/content/E9HR_voxQ2a2tvWUuva_p.md"}